{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus","id":1058527,"title":"The life of a Lupus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-05T12:59:53-08:00","id":1058527,"title":"The life of a Lupus","content":"They are born like wolves, does that mean that they will get the chance to transform to their human form only after their First Change? <br /> <br /> If they are raised by Garou, would they do anything important until their First Change? <br /> <br /> How would they get the knowledge to shapeshift into their Human form? Why would they even want to do it? Is it possible for a Lupus to stay in his natural form, the wolf, during his whole life going to Crinos only in wars and battles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:31:14-08:00","id":1058543,"title":"","content":"Yes, even Metis cannot transform before the First Change. No, probably not, considering they will only be a year old when they experience the First Change. They intuitively gain the knowledge to transform into human form (it is magic), and being human and wolf is part of being a Garou. No, probably not, as losing the human should be considered as bad as losing the wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:07:04-08:00","id":1058592,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ng-lupus-metis</a> This thread has good discussion on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:15:25-08:00","id":1058600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus#post1058527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They are born like wolves, does that mean that they will get the chance to transform to their human form only after their First Change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they are raised by Garou, would they do anything important until their First Change? </div> </div> </div> Sometimes (rarely) hunt beside their Garou family. They only have a year or 2 though, so their time is somewhat limited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would they get the knowledge to shapeshift into their Human form? </div> </div> </div>Being taught. The same way Homids learn to take other forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would they even want to do it? </div> </div> </div>To blend in. To travel through human settlements. To experience new senses. Curiosity. There are a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it possible for a Lupus to stay in his natural form, the wolf, during his whole life going to Crinos only in wars and battles? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Though it's unlikely. The various forms have a number of advantages.<br /> Also worth adding, if the Lupus is that against taking human form, they are probably more comfortable fighting in Hispo rather than Crinos. I've seen a few Lupus characters take that route.<br /> <br /> And slightly related, but worth reading <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/150682893784/anas-guide-to-playing-lupus\" target=\"_blank\">this blog</a> is you want insight into some lupus character stuffs.<br /> Edit: and since she just posted, (sorry) I forgot to make to to credit <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a> for that blog. Good stuff there. There is also one for Metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-05-2017, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:36:09-08:00","id":1058613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058600#post1058600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep.<br /> Sometimes (rarely) hunt beside their Garou family. They only have a year or 2 though, so their time is somewhat limited.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being taught. The same way Homids learn to take other forms.<br /> <br /> <br /> To blend in. To travel through human settlements. To experience new senses. Curiosity. There are a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. Though it's unlikely. The various forms have a number of advantages.<br /> Also worth adding, if the Lupus is that against taking human form, they are probably more comfortable fighting in Hispo rather than Crinos. I've seen a few Lupus characters take that route.<br /> <br /> And slightly related, but worth reading <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/150682893784/anas-guide-to-playing-lupus&amp;quot;]this</a> blog[/URL] is you want insight into some lupus character stuffs.<br /> Edit: and since she just posted, (sorry) I forgot to make to to credit <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> for that blog. Good stuff there. There is also one for Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they more intelligent than normal wolves and do they know that actually they will become humans one day? <br /> Can you please give me the page number in Werewolf The Apocalypse about how much successes I need to shapeshift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:52:26-08:00","id":1058620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058613#post1058613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Are they more intelligent than normal wolves and do they know that actually they will become humans one day?</div> </div> </div> </div>So this one is arguable (and has been argued on these forums). Personal opinion: yes, they are more intelligent than normal wolves. No , they are not of human intelligence. The books speak about leap of logic and making mental connections for Lupus around the time they go through their first change.<br /> <br /> And they wouldn't know about becoming Garou (not human) one day unless they are told about it (by a parent, or Garou relative or a spirit).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058613#post1058613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you please give me the page number in Werewolf The Apocalypse about how much successes I need to shapeshift?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure:<br /> -Revised: starts on page 203 (1 + 1 success for each form shifted, so 5 total successes to go from Homid to Lupus)<br /> -W20: starts on page 285 (1 success for each form shifted, so 4 total successes to go from Homid to Lupus)<br /> <br /> The rules depend on the edition you're playing. They varied slightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:00:39-08:00","id":1058625,"title":"","content":"Are they wolfs in human body or humans in wolf's body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:22:22-08:00","id":1058636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058625#post1058625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they wolfs in human body or humans in wolf's body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh... neither?<br /> <br /> Garou are half-physical, half-spiritual hybrid shapeshifters with traits of both wolves and humans. Whether they are Lupus or Homid born, or Metis, doesn't change this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 03-05-2017, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:27:46-08:00","id":1058638,"title":"","content":"What about eating meat when they are in Lupus form, will they vomit it when they shapshift back into a human? Alive meat, like from deer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:31:03-08:00","id":1058643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058638#post1058638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about eating meat when they are in Lupus form, will they vomit it when they shapshift back into a human? Alive meat, like from deer</div> </div> </div> </div>Not addressed. I just kind of assume if you are full (or hungry) in Lupus, you are full (or hungry) in each form. It's the easiest approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:16:13-08:00","id":1058677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058638#post1058638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about eating meat when they are in Lupus form, will they vomit it when they shapshift back into a human? Alive meat, like from deer</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering I can eat a tartar steak with little problem, it will stay in the stomach just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:17:01-08:00","id":1058680,"title":"","content":"To add onto the previous posts,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus#post1058527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are born like wolves, does that mean that they will get the chance to transform to their human form only after their First Change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. That's why they call it the First Change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus#post1058527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are raised by Garou, would they do anything important until their First Change?</div> </div> </div> </div>Breeding is by far the most important thing a pre-Change Lupus can do. Second to that is protecting their kin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus#post1058527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would they get the knowledge to shapeshift into their Human form?</div> </div> </div> </div>All Cubs need instruction in Shifting, some more than others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus#post1058527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they even want to do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Guns. Grenades. Opposable thumbs in general. Language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T19:05:05-08:00","id":1058735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058677#post1058677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering I can eat a tartar steak with little problem, it will stay in the stomach just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, to emphasize the point again, Garou aren't usually affected by diseases and poison, by virtue of not being entirely physical. They're monsters with power beyond mere flesh, so they don't have to worry about raw meat from roadkill, theobromine poisoning or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T22:20:39-08:00","id":1058781,"title":"","content":"I think they have to worry about poison in their breed form (except Metis), but that is easily fixed with shifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T22:47:33-08:00","id":1058789,"title":"","content":"So I don't have to roll for shapshifting into a Lupus if that is my breed form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T22:52:20-08:00","id":1058791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058789#post1058789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't have to roll for shapshifting into a Lupus if that is my breed form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. You can always shift back to your breed form instantly with no roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T23:09:31-08:00","id":1058795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058781#post1058781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they have to worry about poison in their breed form (except Metis), but that is easily fixed with shifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming that they'd primarily be eating chocolate in Homid form, if at all. It gets rapidly picked apart by the catabolism, and becomes nothing to worry about if they shift back into breed form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T00:26:47-08:00","id":1058809,"title":"","content":"OP might be interested in the Red Talons, who actively despise humanity and tend to stick to Lupus where possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:17:47-08:00","id":1058821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058543#post1058543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, even Metis cannot transform before the First Change...</div> </div> </div> </div>Although it should be noted that Metis with the Metamorph Merit <i>can</i> shapeshift from birth (Fengy from Sept of the Green is named as a specific example). Guardians of the Caerns, page 105.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:32:11-08:00","id":1058825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058791#post1058791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. You can always shift back to your breed form instantly with no roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I do not need to roll to shapeshift into a Lupus but what about shapeshifting from Lupus to Homid? <br /> <br /> Can you describe me the process of shapeshifting... Is it like.. <br /> Jack falls on all four, rapidly growing fur and costure of a large wolf, his whole body changes. <br /> Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:00:39-08:00","id":1058931,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily. The process can be slow or quick. The slow process goes through the intermediary forms and does not require a roll. The quick process skips the intermediary forms and usually requires a roll. During the slow process, you become more and more inhuman over four turns (12 seconds), so your description is roughly what happens during the slow process. During the fast process, you instantly become the form, so the man is replaced by the wolf (just like a magic trick).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:17:33-08:00","id":1058939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058931#post1058931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily. The process can be slow or quick. The slow process goes through the intermediary forms and does not require a roll. The quick process skips the intermediary forms and usually requires a roll. During the slow process, you become more and more inhuman over four turns (12 seconds), so your description is roughly what happens during the slow process. During the fast process, you instantly become the form, so the man is replaced by the wolf (just like a magic trick).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this RAW? <br /> Can you give me the page number for this in Werewolf The Apocalypse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:32:17-08:00","id":1058946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058825#post1058825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So I do not need to roll to shapeshift into a Lupus but what about shapeshifting from Lupus to Homid?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are Lupus Breed, then you need to roll to go to Homid form and you'll need 4 or 5 successes, depending on edition.<br /> <br /> Quick clarification: which edition are we talking about? The wording for this section is different between Revised and W20 and will make it easier to answer some of these questions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058825#post1058825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can you describe me the process of shapeshifting... Is it like..<br /> Jack falls on all four, rapidly growing fur and costure of a large wolf, his whole body changes.<br /> Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly. There are some circumstances that make this description misleading, which is somewhat why I asked about edition.<br /> <br /> Assuming W20 for the moment, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>'s response is mostly correct (imo) but is worth elaborating on.<br /> <br /> By the &quot;slow process&quot;, I'm going to assume he is just using the taking 1 success rule (if you have a dice pool equal to the dif of the roll, you can usually just assume a single success and not roll)? Because otherwise this is misleading (or I could not at least find the section where is states that). Going by that rule, you can shift 1 form automatically a turn if you have at least 6 dice to shapeshift (so Stam+Primal Urge) in Homid form. That would allow you to shift 1 form a turn for 4 turns and get to Lupus automatically. This assumes a Homid Breed character (a Metis would just autoshift to Crinos and then shift from there and a Lupus would just auto-shift to Lupus form).<br /> <br /> Now previous editions mentioned that if you rolled and didn't get enough successes, that you shifted as far as you successes would take you (possibly ending up in Glabro, Crinos or Hispo accidentally). That wording seems to be missing from W20, so it seems to be an all or nothing shift now. You either make it to your target form or you don't. <br /> <br /> Also worth adding, that even if you fail the roll you can always spend Rage afterwards to still instantly go to your desired form if you have the Rage left to spend on the turn. You will just have wasted an action on a failed roll. And Rage expenditure shifting (in each edition) is instantaneous and requires no roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:46:32-08:00","id":1058988,"title":"","content":"I need answers only from this books <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://m.imgur.com/BtloCCY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://m.imgur.com/BtloCCY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://m.imgur.com/BtloCCY\" target=\"_blank\"> http://m.imgur.com/BtloCCY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:08:51-08:00","id":1059026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058988#post1058988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need answers only from this books<br /> <a href=\"http://m.imgur.com/BtloCCY\" target=\"_blank\">http://m.imgur.com/BtloCCY</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. That helps.<br /> <br /> Just ignore the parts of my earlier responses that referred to Revised. The rest should stand as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:25:21-08:00","id":1059031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1058946#post1058946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Now previous editions mentioned that if you rolled and didn't get enough successes, that you shifted as far as you successes would take you (possibly ending up in Glabro, Crinos or Hispo accidentally). That wording seems to be missing from W20, so it seems to be an all or nothing shift now. You either make it to your target form or you don't.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the wording is ambiguous enough to keep this in if you like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:39:10-08:00","id":1059040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1059031#post1059031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the wording is ambiguous enough to keep this in if you like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But was trying to keep my answers as close to RAW as possible since I didn't want them to be confusing (I was guessing that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13055\" data-vbnamecard=\"13055\">Goran.</a>) was a new player.<br /> <br /> I never ran (or played) it with the all or nothing idea, since my group and I are used to the rules from previous editions. Looking up citations for this thread though, it occurred to me that it may not be like that anymore (again, by RAW).<br /> /shrug","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:54:33-08:00","id":1059100,"title":"","content":"Well. I played mage character until now and in community in which I am playing there are all races from 20th anniversary editions all together: Vampires, Werewolves, Hunters, Demons, Vampires, Mages, Numina.. even Hybrids, etc<br /> I'm trying to make my new werewolf character, Ahroun Lupus, Adren or maybe even Fostern","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:32:50-08:00","id":1059122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1059100#post1059100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. I played mage character until now and in community in which I am playing there are all races from 20th anniversary editions all together: Vampires, Werewolves, Hunters, Demons, Vampires, Mages, Numina.. even Hybrids, etc<br /> I'm trying to make my new werewolf character, Ahroun Lupus, Adren or maybe even Fostern</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean any insult. From the questions, it sounded like you were (at least relatively) new to Werewolf, and so I was trying to keep my answers as close to straight forward as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:48:47-08:00","id":1059130,"title":"","content":"No I didn't think it was an insult, don't worry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:17:40-08:00","id":1059660,"title":"","content":"How is one Garou initiated into a tribe? Does that happen after the First Change or immediately after Lupus's birth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:23:06-08:00","id":1059663,"title":"","content":"Usually after the First Change. Since the probability of one of the pups from a wolf litter being Garou ranges from 10%-35% when one parent is Garou (and 1% to 11% when both parents are Kinfolk), there is little reason to initiate a random wolf pup into a tribe when the probability of them becoming Garou ranges from 0.2% to 7% (the average wolf liter contains five pups).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:29:19-08:00","id":1059669,"title":"","content":"Rite of Passage<br /> Any ideas? Is it bad idea that his quest would be to kill group of local hunters(normal human hunters) who killed three normal wolfs? I'm asking for Get of Fenris. <br /> Would that be his initation into the tribe? <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:37:33-08:00","id":1059676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1059660#post1059660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is one Garou initiated into a tribe? Does that happen after the First Change or immediately after Lupus's birth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually at the end of their Rite of Passage.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1059669#post1059669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rite of Passage<br /> Any ideas? Is it bad idea that his quest would be to kill group of local hunters(normal human hunters) who killed three normal wolfs? I'm asking for Get of Fenris.<br /> Would that be his initation into the tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you didn't ask me, but almost certainly not. 3 human hunters isn't any sort of challenge.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 03-07-2017, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T12:49:00-08:00","id":1059692,"title":"","content":"What would be the challenge then? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:03:35-08:00","id":1059698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1059692#post1059692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the challenge then? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a></div> </div> </div> </div>For a Get, it should be some sort of combat.<br /> <br /> You can have it start out as hunting down a trio of hunters, but then it gets bigger/more interesting. Perhaps they are Hunters (capital H). Either Reckoning hunters or more mundane werewolf hunters (using silver). Maybe they're fomori, hunting Garou kin. They can even just be mundane hunters, with a Bane following them around, subtly directing their attacks.<br /> <br /> It's not required, but imo, Rite of Passage should involve some supernatural element. They should at the very least be a serious challenge (whether mental or physical or both). For the more combat focused Garou (Get) this should involve a fight that has a legitimate chance of injuring the Cub. This is the point, where the new Garou proves themselves worthy of Fenris's name. Upon completion there should be no doubt that this child has proved themselves a capable warrior.<br /> <br /> What Auspice is the Garou in question btw.That being factored in can add a lot more flavor to Rite of Passage ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:19:44-08:00","id":1059712,"title":"","content":"Ahroun is his Auspice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:58:08-08:00","id":1059727,"title":"","content":"For an Ahroun, the Rite of Passage could either be according to type (hunt down and kill a group of Fomori who have been polluting the local area without appearing as Crinos in front of any humans) or against type (stop three human hunters from killing local wolves without resorting to violence). In the former case, they will prove their worth as warriors. In the latter case, they will prove their worth as leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:04:58-08:00","id":1059733,"title":"","content":"I choose that his quest is to kill the Hunter who killed girl in hos First Change. I think that is good enough as Hunter almost killed him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:21:50-08:00","id":1059745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1059727#post1059727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an Ahroun, the Rite of Passage could either be according to type (hunt down and kill a group of Fomori who have been polluting the local area without appearing as Crinos in front of any humans) or against type (stop three human hunters from killing local wolves without resorting to violence). In the former case, they will prove their worth as warriors. In the latter case, they will prove their worth as leaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, though I don't know whether I would add the Crinos stipulation. That part is kind of a given with the Litany tenets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1059733#post1059733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I choose that his quest is to kill the Hunter who killed girl in hos First Change. I think that is good enough as Hunter almost killed him?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you were trying to say here, sorry. But if it's a capital &quot;H&quot; hunter then you should be all good. They are legitimate threats to beginning supernatural creatures.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T13:35:43-08:00","id":1060253,"title":"","content":"Can somone give me the page of page with explanation for shapshifting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T14:52:28-08:00","id":1060292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goran.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1058527-the-life-of-a-lupus?p=1060253#post1060253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can somone give me the page of page with explanation for shapshifting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm away from the book, but 285 I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T15:02:21-08:00","id":1060299,"title":"","content":"Yeah, 285. Assuming you mean W20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}